---
import { Footer } from "../../components/Footer";
import SiteHeader from "../../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteIcons from "../../components/SiteIcons.astro";
import ThemeScript from "../../components/ThemeScript.astro";
import "../../styles/tailwind.css";

const link =
  "text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 underline decoration-stone-300 underline-offset-4 hover:text-stone-900 dark:hover:text-stone-100";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <SiteIcons />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>Background - Ryan Johnson</title>
    <ThemeScript />
  </head>
  <body
    class="bg-background text-foreground selection:bg-stone-200 selection:text-stone-900 dark:selection:bg-stone-800 dark:selection:text-stone-100 min-h-screen flex flex-col"
  >
    <SiteHeader items={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Background" }]} />
    <main class="w-full flex-1 mt-8 mb-12">
      <div class="chrome-width">
        <div class="structural-border border-t-0 p-8 md:p-12">
          <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl space-y-12 text-left">
            <header class="space-y-4">
              <h1 class="text-5xl font-heading tracking-tighter">Background</h1>
              <p class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone-500">
                Context / Origins
              </p>
            </header>

            <section class="space-y-4">
              <h2 class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-stone-400 font-normal">
                Core Disciplines
              </h2>
              <ul class="m-0 list-none space-y-2 p-0 text-[11px] font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-stone-500">
                <li>• Computer Science</li>
                <li>• UI/UX</li>
                <li>• Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)</li>
                <li>• Mathematics</li>
                <li>• Physics</li>
              </ul>
            </section>

            <div class="space-y-4">
              <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed font-sans">
                I am a computer scientist with an undergraduate degree from the University of Memphis. In my free time I research computer science, programming languages, human-computer interaction (HCI)—which involves user interface (UI) and user experience (UX) design—and information theory, decision theory, behavioral economics, physics, game theory, cognitive science, neuroscience, psychology, pathology, social science, ecology (in the abstract sense), philosophy, and a limited amount of microbiology (just enough to read research abstracts and skim articles). I also play chess, and my performance level has hovered between 1700 and 1800 for the past year.
              </p>
              <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed font-sans">
                I have a background in physics and mathematics. I earned a 33 composite score on the ACT (out of 36), and a 2000 on the SAT (out of 2400). My top ACT sections were Mathematics (34) and Science (35). I also earned a perfect score on the physics subject test for the SAT in 2007.
              </p>
              <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed font-sans">
                I started programming in early high school on a Texas Instruments TI-83+ Silver Edition calculator, using a structured language called TI-BASIC. My brother taught me how to write a for loop and a while loop, and I immediately recognized how powerful programming could be. I practiced programming several hours a day every day for 3 years. I developed a fractal generator on the calculator using imaginary numbers and iterative math (iterated function systems), as well as a black and white image compression algorithm, and I regularly programmed my calculator to do my math homework for me. TI BASIC was a primitive programming language. It provided no lexical scoping for variables, so all variables were accessible from all programs, making it difficult to guard the program from unwanted environment changes. When encountering a bug, the program editor would scroll all the way down to the line it errored on, so I had to write programs in reverse to speed up the debugging process. The calculator could only display 8 lines of text and 16 characters across, so I had to memorize all of my code.
              </p>
              <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed font-sans italic">
                I am an &ldquo;unprofessional&rdquo;: I do not respect the traditions of the profession. I break
                expectations and question the existing order of things.
              </p>
              <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed font-sans">
                My attitude toward professionalism is formed in part through the influences of leaders and mavericks across various disciplines, seen on the{" "}
                <a href="/inspirations" class={link}>Inspirations page</a>. You can browse my philosophy on the{" "}
                <a href="/philosophy" class={link}>Philosophy page</a>. You can visit my blog articles on this site from the{" "}
                <a href="/blog" class={link}>blog</a>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>

    <Footer client:load />
  </body>
</html>
